  "title": "SEC Transfer Agent Modernization — 2026 Proposal",
  "question": "How would the SEC's 2026 transfer-agent proposal govern authoritative securityholder records across electronic, blockchain and multichain systems while preserving accountable legal control?",
  "bluf": "The SEC's September 1 proposal would permit an authoritative master securityholder file to use multiple linked electronic systems, including a blockchain or DLT as the file or a component, while retaining one registered recordkeeping transfer agent responsible for and in exclusive control of each fungible issue. It turns tokenization into a reportable, governed operating model rather than approving any chain, company or token. The exact comment deadline remains pending Federal Register publication.",
